# Intent: stop the robot's repeating plug-in/unplug beeps and make every cue attributable (owner 2026-11-14: "it never did that before"). A Fable review found patch 117's 1 s power poll fed the sounds from IsExternalPowerConnected(), upstream power-save code (battery current direction != discharging) that flips with the servo load on battery and with a weak USB supply, so the unit played plug_in and unplug pairs about once or twice a minute, idle and dancing. The sounds now use the AXP2101 VBUS-good bit (status 1, register 0x00, bit 5) OR charging, a change must hold 10 s (20 s for "cable pulled out"), a per-cue minimum gap in the unit's gate refuses a repeat (plug_in 30 s, low_battery 10 min, shutter 1.5 s, ...), the host is told which cue played and what asked for it (device event "sound_played"), and once a minute it hears the charger reading and the flap count (diag event "power_poll").
# Check after a flash: the log shows `sound played: <name> (<src>)` for every cue; the host log shows `sound_played` events; on a cable with a weak supply or on battery no plug_in/unplug repeats; core test: body/tests/firmware/sounds_core_test.c (flap and gap cases).
